WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.667
-Thank you for being here. I'm such a big fan.

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:05.000
-Oh, likewise.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.901
But also I'm particularly glad that you're not dead.

00:00:06.901 --> 00:00:08.367
-Thank you.

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:09.534
-Because I don't know if you know this,

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:11.000
but you actually saved my life once.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.334
So thank you.

00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:14.200
-Did I really? -You really did.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.501
This is actually a true story.

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:19.701
It's pretty cuckoo bananas. As are my shoes.

00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:20.934
I'm just saying.

00:00:20.934 --> 00:00:23.200
-No, these are fantastic. Can we see these?

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.367
These are gorgeous. -I have golden toes.

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:27.467
I don't know why, but okay.

00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:29.534
-Yeah. No. They're gorgeous. I love them.

00:00:29.534 --> 00:00:33.133
-On the subject of kind of insane fashion,

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.767
it was at the Met Gala.

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:36.534
My first and only time being there.

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:39.701
I was wearing a dress that was ridiculously heavy,

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:41.133
and I couldn't really move

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:43.033
and I was just kind of trying to get through the evening.

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:46.634
And at the end of the night, I'm at the top of the stairs.

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:49.267
The gorgeous Hailee Steinfeld walks past me,

00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:53.300
has a very complicated, like, three-train thing,

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:54.634
and I get wrapped up in it.

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:56.801
And I'm like, "Oh, I'm going to die.

00:00:56.801 --> 00:01:00.567
I'm going to die on the steps of the Met, darling."

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:02.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.234 --> 00:01:04.200
But literally just out of nowhere,

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.801
the "hand of God" came out

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:07.701
and pulled me out of it, and it was you.

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:10.000
And you were just so sweet about it.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.133
You were like, "Hey, I'm Jimmy. Nice to meet you."

00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:13.968
I was like, "Okay."

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:15.834
-Yeah. Yeah. That's exactly right.

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:17.367
-So thank you, Jimmy Fallon.

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:18.767
-No big deal. -Thank you.

00:01:18.767 --> 00:01:20.701
-I do remember that. You were going down.

00:01:20.701 --> 00:01:22.901
-Yeah. And you were next to Sarah Paulson.

00:01:22.901 --> 00:01:24.901
And from that moment on, my night got so much better

00:01:24.901 --> 00:01:26.801
'cause I actually knew somebody there.

00:01:26.801 --> 00:01:28.234
-Yeah. So we had fun. Oh, good.

00:01:28.234 --> 00:01:31.000
I'm so happy you're here and saved your life.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.167
I probably told you,

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:33.901
but I love you in "The Queen's Gambit."

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:36.200
I thought you were so great. You were unbelievable.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.167
[ Cheers and applause ] Congrats on every award.

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:39.601
-Thank you.

00:01:39.601 --> 00:01:41.767
-Congrats on every award you got for that thing.

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:44.000
I really loved every second of your acting in that.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.167
I go, "Oh, my gosh. Can't take my eyes off you."

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:48.367
-Thanks. -You were telling me backstage

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:51.033
that you kind of owe your career to the Beach Boys.

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:52.434
-Yeah.

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:56.033
-So, now, walk me through that, how that's real.

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:58.501
-Well -- How that's real? -Yeah.

00:01:58.501 --> 00:02:01.067
-So, I grew up listening to the music

00:02:01.067 --> 00:02:02.968
of the '50s and the '60s. -Me too.

00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:05.200
-That was just, like, my literal jam.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.934
And they were playing, and I just had to --

00:02:08.934 --> 00:02:12.200
I just ran to the very front and was singing my heart out.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:15.234
And Mike Love stopped the concert and said,

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:18.834
"I understand why all of you know all the words to the songs,

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:20.501
but there's a literal child

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:22.968
that is singing, like, every single song.

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:24.934
I'd like to invite her up on stage."

00:02:24.934 --> 00:02:25.968
[ Audience awws ]

00:02:25.968 --> 00:02:27.300
And, like, pulled me up -- I know.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.968
It's the coolest thing that will ever happen to me.

00:02:28.968 --> 00:02:32.267
I peaked at 14. It's the end from now on.

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:33.968
But, yeah, he pulled me up on stage

00:02:33.968 --> 00:02:35.367
and then handed me a guitar.

00:02:35.367 --> 00:02:37.300
And I looked at him, and I was like,

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.167
"I don't know how to play the guitar."

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:40.567
He's like, "No, no. Just go for it."

00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:43.667
So I air-guitared like crazy.

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:46.534
The solo was out of this world. -Yes.

00:02:46.534 --> 00:02:49.868
You air-guitared -- You actually have a photo of you.

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:51.267
[ Audience awws ]

00:02:51.267 --> 00:02:54.601
-look at the face, though. I'm doing nothing.

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:56.300
-You really are --

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:59.033
[ Cheers and applause ] You look great.

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:02.934
So how did this, which is a cool moment in life,

00:03:02.934 --> 00:03:05.501
lead to acting and your career?

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:07.367
-Well, then I got scouted for modeling,

00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:10.400
which is something I never thought I could do.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:11.801
Always wanted to act.

00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:14.334
So, I brought the video of this, and I asked them

00:03:14.334 --> 00:03:16.300
if they believed that I could play the guitar.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:17.834
And they were like, "Yeah, you're shredding it."

00:03:17.834 --> 00:03:19.567
I was like, "Acting."

00:03:19.567 --> 00:03:20.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.968 --> 00:03:22.767
-"See? I don't even know how to play the guitar!"

00:03:22.767 --> 00:03:26.200
-Let me do this.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:28.133
-Fans are very excited about this.

00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:29.734
You're in the new "Super Mario Bros. movie."

00:03:29.734 --> 00:03:31.334
This is a big deal. -Yeah.

00:03:31.334 --> 00:03:33.400
-Princess Peach. -Yes, sir.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.200
-That's a big deal. And, uh...

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:41.033
I saw this -- I thought this was very fun and very cool of you.

00:03:41.033 --> 00:03:43.767
On Halloween, you dressed as Princess Peach.

00:03:43.767 --> 00:03:46.267
Did people freak out? Did they go nuts?

00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:48.767
-I mean, yes, but, like, the story of this

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:54.634
is that I've been in the desert in Australia for seven months

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:57.734
doing things that are very not Princess Peach

00:03:57.734 --> 00:04:00.133
on "Mad Max: Furiosa." -That's right.

00:04:00.133 --> 00:04:02.467
-So I had landed back from Australia that morning,

00:04:02.467 --> 00:04:04.400
and I had agreed to go to this Halloween party,

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.067
but I thought it would be on Halloween.

00:04:06.067 --> 00:04:07.501
And so I get a text that morning.

00:04:07.501 --> 00:04:09.267
They're like, "Hey, I'll see you tonight."

00:04:09.267 --> 00:04:11.767
I was, like, not prepared, no outfit, no nothing.

00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:13.567
I have no idea what I'm gonna do.

00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:15.267
So I had that pink dress.

00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:17.801
A friend of mine sewed the button.

00:04:17.801 --> 00:04:20.167
And found one of the many crowns

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:23.534
I have around my apartment and put it on.

00:04:23.534 --> 00:04:25.300
No. A gas station. -And that's how you became --

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:26.634
-And then -- Yeah, Princess Peach.

00:04:26.634 --> 00:04:28.033
-There you go. That's how you do it.

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:30.534
See? You're making a Princess Peach costume quick.

00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:32.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:32.634 --> 00:04:34.601
-Can we talk about "the menu"?

00:04:34.601 --> 00:04:36.267
-Yes. -I love this movie.

00:04:36.267 --> 00:04:39.334
It's so -- It's one of those movies where I didn't know

00:04:39.334 --> 00:04:42.334
where it was going to go at all or what was going to happen.

00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:44.467
And I don't want to spoil anything for anyone.

00:04:44.467 --> 00:04:47.033
How would you describe this?

00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:50.200
-Much like the shoes, potentially cuckoo bananas.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:51.601
I don't even know if that's a phrase.

00:04:51.601 --> 00:04:53.234
-Cuckoo bananas. -I started saying it today.

00:04:53.234 --> 00:04:55.868
Is it cuckoo bananas or cuckoo banana puffs?

00:04:55.868 --> 00:04:59.033
Like, what would you -- -How would I say it?

00:04:59.033 --> 00:05:02.167
"That's so cuckoo banana puffs." -Cuckoo banana puffs.

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:03.501
-"Cuckoo bananas" is great.

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:06.834
-The movie is about a couple that signs up

00:05:06.834 --> 00:05:10.167
to a very exclusive restaurant on an island.

00:05:10.167 --> 00:05:13.567
And it's supposed to be, you know, for the 1% of the 1%.

00:05:13.567 --> 00:05:17.100
And, very quickly, things go awry.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:19.734
But it is bitingly funny.

00:05:19.734 --> 00:05:21.501
I've been trying to get through this press tour,

00:05:21.501 --> 00:05:24.033
like, inserting as many food puns as I can.

00:05:24.033 --> 00:05:26.801
-Oh. "Bitingly." -Bitingly funny.

00:05:26.801 --> 00:05:28.467
-Also cuckoo bananas is a little --

00:05:28.467 --> 00:05:30.067
-Cuckoo bananas, yeah.

00:05:30.067 --> 00:05:32.534
-It's fun. It's funny.

00:05:32.534 --> 00:05:34.434
Ralph Fiennes, by the way. Brilliant.

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:35.901
-I know. -It's really good.

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:37.367
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:37.367 --> 00:05:39.334
Here's Anya Taylor-Joy in "The Menu."

00:05:39.334 --> 00:05:42.434
Take a look at this.

00:05:42.434 --> 00:05:45.000
-There's only one more savory course left in our menu.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.467
That means we must prepare for dessert.

00:05:47.467 --> 00:05:49.300
Dessert requires a large barrel

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:52.267
that is supposed to be there in the corner.

00:05:52.267 --> 00:05:54.934
Do you see a barrel?

00:05:54.934 --> 00:05:56.868
-No. No, I do not. -Neither do I.

00:05:56.868 --> 00:05:59.434
That is because my negligent colleague, Elsa,

00:05:59.434 --> 00:06:02.801
forgot to assign someone to bring it.

00:06:02.801 --> 00:06:06.434
So, Margot, you will fetch the barrel instead.

00:06:06.434 --> 00:06:07.701
-Me? -Yes.

00:06:07.701 --> 00:06:10.000
You remember the smokehouse.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.567
-Maybe -- Vague-- I don't --

00:06:11.567 --> 00:06:13.300
-Chef, perhaps one of us should --

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:16.133
-Margot is now one of us, Elsa.

00:06:16.133 --> 00:06:18.167
Right, Margot?

00:06:18.167 --> 00:06:20.734
-Yes. -Yes, what?

00:06:20.734 --> 00:06:22.868
-Yes, Chef.

00:06:22.868 --> 00:06:25.400
-Yes! [ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:27.400
Anya Taylor-Joy, everyone!

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.367
"The Menu" is in theaters this Friday.

00:06:30.367 --> 00:06:33.100
Anya and I are doing something fun after the break.

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:34.467
Stick around, everybody!

